Task 3: Requirements Traceability Matrix (RTM) – Order Placement Flow

 1. Objective

The objective of this task is to create a Requirements Traceability Matrix (RTM) for the Order Placement feature of a food delivery application.

RTM helps to connect functional requirements with test scenarios and identified defects. It ensures that all requirements are properly covered by testing.

 2. Functional Requirements

FR_01 – Add Item to Cart
- The user should be able to add food items to the cart.
- The cart should display the selected items and their prices.

FR_02 – Apply Coupon
- The user should be able to apply a valid coupon code.
- The system should calculate and display the correct discount.

FR_03 – Select Payment Method
- The user should be able to select a payment method such as UPI, Credit Card, Debit Card, or Cash on Delivery.

FR_04 – Place Order
- The user should be able to place an order after completing all required steps.
- The system should create the order successfully.

FR_05 – View Order Confirmation
- The system should display an order confirmation screen after successful order placement.
- The confirmation screen should show the correct order details.

FR_06 – View Order History
- The user should be able to view previously placed orders.
- The system should display correct order details and order status.

3. Test Scenarios

FR_01 – Add Item to Cart

- TS_01: Verify that the user can successfully add a food item to the cart.
- TS_02: Verify that the cart displays the correct item name, quantity, and price.

FR_02 – Apply Coupon

- TS_03: Verify that the user can successfully apply a valid coupon code.
- TS_04: Verify that the system displays an appropriate error message for an invalid or expired coupon.

FR_03 – Select Payment Method

- TS_05: Verify that the user can select UPI as a payment method.
- TS_06: Verify that the user can select Cash on Delivery as a payment method.

FR_04 – Place Order

- TS_07: Verify that the user can successfully place an order after selecting a valid payment method.
- TS_08: Verify that the system does not place an order when required information is missing.

FR_05 – View Order Confirmation

- TS_09: Verify that the order confirmation screen is displayed after successful order placement.
- TS_10: Verify that the confirmation screen displays the correct order ID, total amount, and delivery address.

FR_06 – View Order History

- TS_11: Verify that the user can view previously placed orders.
- TS_12: Verify that the order history displays the correct order details and status.

