5. Defect Details

The following are hypothetical defects created for this assignment.

DEF_01 – Cart Price Mismatch
- Requirement ID: FR_01
- Test Scenario ID: TS_02
- Severity: S2 – High
- Description: The cart displays an incorrect total price after adding multiple food items.

DEF_02 – Coupon Discount Not Applied
- Requirement ID: FR_02
- Test Scenario ID: TS_03
- Severity: S2 – High
- Description: The system accepts a valid coupon code but does not apply the discount to the order total.

DEF_03 – Order Placed Without Required Information
- Requirement ID: FR_04
- Test Scenario ID: TS_08
- Severity: S1 – Critical
- Description: The system allows the user to place an order without entering the required delivery address.

6. Severity Classification

- S1 – Critical: A defect that causes major application failure or blocks an important business operation.
- S2 – High: A defect that seriously affects important functionality.
- S3 – Medium: A defect that affects functionality but has a workaround.
- S4 – Low: A minor defect that has very little impact on application functionality.

 7. Conclusion

RTM helps testers track all functional requirements and ensures that each requirement has proper test coverage. 
Forward Traceability connects requirements with test scenarios and related defects.
It also helps identify missing test scenarios and ensures that important requirements are tested properly.
